WavesFit is a new Python/Go implementation informed by a collection of 29 local Igor Pro
procedure files. Redistribution and an MIT license were authorized by the supplying user.
The original laboratory contributors are not identified reliably in the supplied files;
the historical description "Luca procedures" is not treated as verified authorship.
Original procedure filenames and byte hashes are recorded in shared/igor-inventory.json.
Original proprietary application code and application binaries are not redistributed.

Scientific references present in the supplied procedure comments:
- Stöhr, NEXAFS Spectroscopy (asymmetric Gaussian and Gaussian step procedures).
- D. A. Shirley, Physical Review B 5 (1972), 4709.
- S. Tougaard, Surface Science 216 (1989), 343.
- V. Lucarini, J. J. Saarinen, K.-E. Peiponen, E. M. Vartiainen,
  Kramers-Kronig Relations in Optical Materials Research, Springer, 2005.
  The related Kramers-Kronig procedure is inventoried but deferred beyond v0.1.0.

Python depends on NumPy and SciPy, which carry their own BSD and bundled dependency notices.
Go depends on Gonum and gospecfunc under BSD licenses. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.
The offline dashboard is original code and has no external JavaScript dependencies.
